/GameBeastProductions/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nCloses #124195.\r\n\r\nThis fixes a shader compilation error when both \"refraction\" and \"proximity fade\" are enabled in a material.\r\n\r\nThis is what was happening before:\r\n<img width=\"3393\" height=\"1859\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9025dc0c-4932-4772-9e14-4ff5e69f1a0d\" />\r\n\r\nAnd this is how it looks with these changes:\r\n<img width=\"3390\" height=\"1868\" alt=\"Screenshot_20261005_211407\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f3f1f071-8ca6-4b25-a7fb-1b895d810121\" />\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThe `ndc` variables in both snippets of shader code have simply been renamed based on the feature they are for.  This ensures that both snippets can be included without causing conflicts.\r\n\r\nThe changes have been tested against the MRP from the linked issue: [RefractionProximityFadeTest.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33071985/RefractionProximityFadeTest.zip).","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9959029909,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAACUZq8lQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/cherrypick:4.6","name":"cherrypick:4.6","description":"Consider